/-!
# Finite-tail exact-MSA extension: certified scope

Pure fluid: faithful BH dictionary; actual Baxter Laplace transform; exterior
closure under the first BH equations; core convolution closed form; smooth
spatial core; existence of a smooth real BH root family near zero coupling.

Mixtures: independent finite species/tail indices, unequal additive diameters,
integrability of the actual real-space convolution, BH dictionary and its
smoothness, actual positive-s Laplace transform, and exterior closure under
the first BH equations. A local smooth real amplitude family through the
constructed PY seed is now proved for positive rates/diameters, nonnegative
species densities and positive mixture free volume. The actual Jacobian,
its distinct diagonal blocks, both determinant conditions and the seed
equation are discharged internally. Actual full-line complex Q/Fourier,
including negative support edges, and actual Q cross-correlation transforms
are now identified. Their marginal weighted L1 discharges joint Fubini L1.
The actual density-weighted Q Gram matrix is positive semidefinite, positive
definite if its factor is invertible, with its density/transposition convention
proved. The Q-side spectral coefficient is Hermitian; reality is equivalent
to species reciprocity. It is also identified with the actual full-line Baxter primitive
transform. The lower-edge derivative correction is proved, and its positive-r
partner vanishes when the larger-diameter species is the row. Actual BH
family Dt slopes are identified with the internally invertible HS block,
and actual exterior DCF slopes are identified with the prescribed tail.
At a BH root and symmetric K, actual exterior primitive reciprocity is
proved on both sides; its species-antisymmetric support is confined to the
finite core, and actual spectral antisymmetry is a finite-core integral.
Actual Q and Qprime now have finite basis expansions; their improper
convolution is a finite quadratic amplitude expression. The actual DCF is
C-infinity in amplitudes at each fixed position, including spatial knots.
Its explicit first variation at the PY seed is proved on the ordered
positive core as well as outside contact, with the G derivative eliminated
internally. Strength superposition and the prescribed exterior follow.
Identification of this first variation with the independent double-propagator
FMSA construction is now proved throughout the ordered positive core and
exterior off contact, hence a.e. on the positive axis. Arbitrary nonzero-root
radial DCF/core reciprocity and nonlinear matrix RDF/OZ reconstruction remain open.
Actual ordered shell integrals and the improper cosine/sine identity are
proved with all analytic conditions internal. Every diagonal species DCF
has its actual radial Fourier coefficient identified at a supplied root.
For arbitrary pairs, a.e. finite-core primitive reciprocity plus per-label K
symmetry supplies the actual ordered radial coefficient, density-weighted
matrix Gram factorization and its positive semidefiniteness at nonzero k.
Core reciprocity is an explicit remaining premise, not inferred from the
root or from Gram positivity. Raw closed-window representatives may have
isolated support-knot spikes; a certified unequal-size HS example rules out
an unnecessary pointwise reciprocity requirement. The actual zero-Dt Q and
primitive are bridged pointwise to the independent general-N HS construction.
At strictly positive species densities the actual PY seed is reciprocal a.e.,
and its all-pair actual radial factorization/PSD needs no core symmetry premise.
The full-space primitive has a fixed finite quadratic basis expansion. Its
explicit first variation along the actual smooth PY BH family exists at all
positions, including support knots, with the G derivative eliminated internally.
Its actual Fourier transform is integrable and equals the derivative of the
Q-product spectral coefficient, for all real wave numbers. The joint family
capstone retains no derivative-existence or integral-interchange premise.
The actual Q tangent now has an explicit two-sided HS factor decomposition,
including its compact quadratic correction. Symmetric per-label K cancels
the cross term in the actual primitive spectral tangent. L1 Fourier
injectivity internally yields full-line first-order primitive a.e. reciprocity
and a.e. evenness, also with zero-density species. Actual Fourier integrals of
the independent fourterm DP W now recover its primitive as actual P1 a.e.
Finite increments and decay fix the integration constant without a first-moment
premise. Spatial odd polarization and DP convolution continuity identify actual
ordered radial c1 with independent dpCorrelation in the entire core/exterior
off contact. The canonical larger-diameter row gives every physical pair.
Actual first-order radial Fourier coefficients equal the actual Baxter product
slope for nonzero k, with radius-weighted L1 internal. These results are not
matrix RDF/OZ recovery or reciprocity of arbitrary nonzero-coupling BH roots.

The spectral algebra blocks are now connected to actual convolution integrals,
their actual sine transforms and the actual Q cosine/sine transforms. Full
scalar finite-tail factorization and nonnegative structure denominator are
proved for positive rates and nonzero wave number. The g-side OZ bridge retains
RDF support, weighted RDF moment integrability, moment identification and the
OZ primitive; it discharges the concrete Baxter kernel's L1 and transform.
A unique actual global Volterra moment is constructed. Normalization cancels
the linear background in its excess equation. An explicit exponential weighted
kernel norm below one internally supplies excess decay and L1. Actual complex
Laplace transfer, Abel boundary and radial Fourier identification then yield
actual Fourier OZ. The radial Fubini/injection bridge discharges all regularity
premises and gives actual radial OZ a.e., jointly with h=-1 inside the core.
At nonzero k its structure denominator is strictly positive in this certified
region. A supplied BH root plus actual excess L1 also suffices. An arbitrary
root alone still does not certify labelled Q/G moments: an exact noncanonical
root obstruction is proved. No all-parameter stability, global-root, RDF
nonnegativity, pressure-loop or coexistence guarantee is asserted.
The actual first-order mixture RDF now has a joint conditional certificate:
two causal matrix Volterra steps construct h1 with pointwise hard-core zero;
actual phase-preserving Laplace/radial Fourier integrals and actual HS c0
factorization yield first-order OZ. Radial Fubini and injectivity recover the
actual radial OZ a.e. The supplied HS reference is an actual function with
hard core, a.e. radial OZ, and a measurable global h0 radius moment. The
actual HS c0 radius L1 is internal from its bounded compact numerator.
Decay of the final constructed Uc supplies Yc L1 internally; an explicit
positive exponential weighted entry-sum budget below one discharges Uc L1
and yields bounds for both actual Volterra stages. The criterion is sufficient,
not necessary, and is identified with explicit finite core integrals. This capstone requires strictly positive species densities under
the current HS reference certificate. At equal diameters the actual HS
reference is independently constructed as baxterPsi at total density divided
by radius. Its actual canonical c0 dictionary and global radius L1 are proved;
the same matrix budget supplies the scalar HS budget internally. The equal-size
capstone therefore takes no supplied h0/reference/decay premise. The actual pair-contact
HS Volterra candidate uses r=R_ij+u, true compact core forcing and the same
left-density Kc transpose. Its actual full-support exterior renewal, pointwise
pair core and global radius L1 are proved under A_delta<1. Actual source
Laplace integrals and HS column moments complete the causal transfer. A
phase-preserving finite-symbol identity, with its physical coefficient relation
proved, gives actual Fourier OZ. Actual canonical c0 convolution smoothing
and radial Fubini/injectivity give radial OZ a.e. Thus all four reference
fields are internal for arbitrary positive additive diameters, strictly
positive densities and positive free volume under the sufficient budget.
The corresponding finite-tail first-order capstone takes no supplied h0,
reference OZ, decay or inverse-transform premise; it additionally requires
delta<=each tail rate. No common-core generic seed theorem is instantiated.
A zero-density open-interval diagnostic shows why a larger common-core
trial cannot replace pair contacts; this is not a positive-density physical
counterexample or a refutation of generic conditional seed theorems.
The actual pairwise full-space seed has both density weights retained;
it vanishes at each own contact and beyond. Its positive-axis canonical
c0 identity is reduced to an explicit a.e. finite-open-core WT premise.
That particular WT identity remains unproved and is not used by the completed
independent actual Fourier route to the valid HS reference.
No all-state decay, contact identity,
nonlinear RDF, stability or zero-k thermodynamic conclusion is asserted.

-/

